    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Decatur is Morgan County's economic engine — a city defined by its Tennessee River access, its industrial base, and its residential neighborhoods that range from pre-war historic homes in the Kingsway district to newer subdivisions in the Beltline Road corridor. BamaClean has served Decatur since 1993, and we understand the city's distinct cleaning and restoration landscape better than any out-of-town competitor can.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Decatur's position at the midpoint of the Tennessee River makes it particularly susceptible to the flooding events that characterize the river system. Point Mallard Park and the areas along the river bottom have flooded repeatedly, and residential areas adjacent to Flint Creek and its tributaries see water intrusion during heavy rain events that the drainage infrastructure cannot always handle. We've performed water damage restoration in Decatur homes during multiple significant weather events — and our familiarity with the city's flood-risk geography helps us scope jobs accurately from the first call.</p>
    <p>The industrial character of Decatur — anchored by GE Appliances and 3M, with a manufacturing corridor that stretches along the Tennessee River industrial district — also creates commercial cleaning demand that we've served for decades. Decatur's workforce families are practical, value-oriented, and skeptical of hype. That's a customer base we've built a business around: deliver what you quote, do it right, and let the results speak.</p>
